Z||000000||Dan86gt3.8||10-26-2000||11:46 PM||||OK I was driving tonight and all of a sudden the idiot light on the voltmeter pops on at first I didn't know what to make of it then I noticed my temp climbing.  sure enough when I went back there and poped the decklid it was gone!  I got the car back to a frinds house.  We then were driving back down the same road and picked up the belt.  It had axle grease on it from last time the cv boot came off.  It also looked like the ac compressor might have ben cockeyed.  I have also ben getting some rattling/vibration noise when I put the car in reverse.  I do not know what to make of all this but It was dark and too late to try to figure out anything else.  I can get the car home tomrow into the parking lot of my apartments so i can work on it.  Umm is there anyhing that causes this typically?  What should I use to clean the grease off the belt and pulleys?  Like alchol, acetone, thinner?  has this ever happened to you?  The belt seems to be fine just dirty and greasy....<P>thanks for any info!<P>------------------<BR>86 gt fiero<BR>3.8/4speed auto<BR>ace conversion kit<BR>1/4- 15.3@90mph||||reg||1
Z||000001||terryk||10-27-2000||01:30 AM||||Check for a loose water pump pulley or a bad tensioner.||||reg||1
Z||000002||robertjay||10-27-2000||07:59 AM||||Mine did it to me once when my alternator pulley came loose.  It would make a heckuva vibration at a certain rpm, so it was quite noticeable, and easy to fix.  As far as cleaning the belt and pulleys, I would use contact cleaner on the pulleys and replace the belt.  Good luck!||||reg||1
Z||000003||Dan86gt3.8||10-27-2000||11:44 AM||||Turns out the ac pump came loose and was just dangling... need to find the right bolts somewhere and bolt it back on put the belt back on.  ||||reg||1
